<article class="env-definition" id="010Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/010Z">Definition <span data-tag="010Z">12.13.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A morphism of chain complexes $f : A_\bullet \to B_\bullet $ is called a <em>quasi-isomorphism</em> if the induced map $H_ i(f) : H_ i(A_\bullet ) \to H_ i(B_\bullet )$ is an isomorphism for all $i \in \mathbf{Z}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A chain complex $A_\bullet $ is called <em>acyclic</em> if all of its homology objects $H_ i(A_\bullet )$ are zero. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>